Issue 7: high ping / large or unnecessary server packets

What was inspected
------------------
- Unpacked versions/26.3/server-26.3.jar (7,762 classes, 166 clientbound
  game packets, 69 serverbound game packets) into .agent-work/tmp/serverjarall
  and inspected the packet classes with javap.
- Reviewed the existing mod set: Krypton already optimizes the Netty pipeline,
  and ServerCore optimizes server ticking. Neither culls unnecessary game
  packets.
- Saved a reproducible analysis at:
  .agent-work/outputs/issue-7-server-jar-analysis.txt
  .agent-work/outputs/issue-7-packet-analysis.md

Implemented changes
-------------------
- Added server-side mod: mods/ultron-network-optimizer-1.0.0.jar
  * Culls far-away particles, positional sounds, block-entity data,
    non-global level events, and block events.
  * Keeps music/UI/voice sounds and important particles
    (overrideLimiter/alwaysShow).
  * Deduplicates repeated block updates for the same position/state.
  * Drops empty entity-data packets.
  * Logs suppressed-packet totals every 300 seconds.
- Added reproducible source and build script under network-optimizer/.
- Added config/ultron-network.properties with per-filter toggles/distances.
- server.properties:
  * view-distance 10 -> 6
  * simulation-distance 10 -> 6
  * entity-broadcast-range-percentage 100 -> 60
  * network-compression-threshold 256 -> 128
- scripts/network-tune.sh:
  * tcp_notsent_lowat=16384
  * net.core.netdev_max_backlog=16384
- README.md documents the mod, config and tuning.
- Added .agent-work/tests/test_network_optimizer.sh and
  .agent-work/tools/analyze-server-jar.sh.

Validation performed
--------------------
- bash network-optimizer/build.sh succeeded.
- .agent-work/tests/test_network_optimizer.sh passed: jar contents, manifest
  mapping namespace, mixin target methods, and a real disposable server start
  with no mixin injection errors.
- .agent-work/tests/test_run.sh passed (server listening after 14s).
- .agent-work/tests/test_network_tune.sh passed; BBR/fq and all TCP settings
  applied successfully.
- bash -n and shellcheck pass for the new/changed shell scripts.

Remaining notes
---------------
- This reduces bandwidth, burst size, and server-side packet work. It cannot
  remove the physical RTT between the US GitHub Actions runner and Bangladesh.
- If stutter remains, the next step is hosting closer to the players.
